<% content_for :title, "Pricing" %>
<% content_for :description, "Free for one person and twenty documents. Alerts and renewal playbooks are never paywalled." %>

<h1>Pricing</h1>

<p class="lede">
  Storage is what costs us money, so storage is what the plans limit.
  <strong>Alerts and playbooks are never paywalled</strong> — putting the safety feature behind a
  card form would poison the trust the whole thing rests on.
</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Free</h3>
    <p class="headline">£0</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>1 person</li>
      <li>20 documents</li>
      <li>Every alert</li>
      <li>Every renewal playbook</li>
      <li>Encrypted scans</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Household</h3>
    <p class="headline">~£4<span class="note">/month</span></p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Up to 6 people</li>
      <li>Unlimited documents</li>
      <li>Shared alerts across the household</li>
      <li>Priority notification channels</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Self-hosted</h3>
    <p class="headline">£0</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Everything, on your own machine</li>
      <li>One container</li>
      <li>Your data never touches us</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note"><a href="https://github.com/cdrrazan/Docaru">Run it yourself</a></p>
  </div>
</div>

<section>
  <h2>What happens if you stop paying</h2>
  <p>
    You keep every reminder for every document you already have. You lose the ability to add more
    people and more documents until you are back under the free limits. Nobody misses a visa
    deadline over a failed card payment — that would be the product failing at the only job it has.
  </p>
</section>

<% if authenticated? %>
  <section>
    <h2>Your plan</h2>
    <p>
      <%= @household.name %> is on the <strong><%= @household.plan.humanize.downcase %></strong> plan,
      using <%= pluralize(@household.documents.count, "document") %> and
      <%= pluralize(@household.members.count, "person") %>.
    </p>

    <% if (subscription = @household.subscription)&.troubled? %>
      <div class="banner banner-warn">
        <strong>There is a problem with the payment for this household.</strong>
        Paddle will retry the card over the next few days. <strong>Every reminder keeps
        working throughout</strong>, and it keeps working even if the payment never succeeds —
        nobody misses a visa deadline over a card.
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% if @household.over_document_limit? || @household.over_member_limit? %>
      <div class="banner">
        This household is above the free limits. Nothing has been deleted and everything is still
        watched — you cannot add anything new until you are back under, or back on the household
        plan.
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% if @household.plan == "free" %>
      <% if Paddle.configured? %>
        <%= button_to "Upgrade to the household plan", plan_path, method: :patch, class: "btn" %>
        <p class="note">
          Checkout is handled by Paddle, who are the seller of record and will show the price in
          your own currency with any tax already included.
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <div class="banner">
          Billing is not switched on for this instance, so there is nothing behind this button and
          it is not shown. Every alert and every playbook works regardless — those are never
          paywalled.
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% elsif subscription&.renews_on %>
      <p class="note">
        <%= subscription.canceled_at ? "Access continues until" : "Renews on" %>
        <%= subscription.renews_on.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
